    "long_instructions": "<p>After exploring user testing and product development decisions in Lesson 11, students move into ethics in Lesson 12, engaging with scenarios where different ethical approaches to AI and computing systems come into play. The video below highlights some of the ethical considerations of AI to help you support this lesson.</p>\r\n\r\nEthics plays a major role in how AI and computing systems are developed, used, and regulated. As AI becomes more common in everyday life, questions about privacy, fairness, safety, and responsibility become increasingly important.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color:#F7F7FB; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:8px; padding:12px 16px; margin:20px 0;\">\r\n<p>📖 <strong>Ethics</strong> helps to guide responsible choices about emerging technologies, ensuring privacy, consent, and safety for everyone.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\nAfter watching this video, students will explore real-world scenarios where ethical questions arise and consider how different stakeholders, such as developers, users, and affected communities, might view these issues.\r\n\r\n## Think About\r\n\r\nAs you watch, reflect on:\r\n\r\n<p>• What computer system in the video might raise ethical concerns for some people?</p>\r\n<p>• What are those concerns?</p>\r\n<p>• How can you deepen students' understanding of data ethics, bias, or interpretation in future lessons?</p>\r\n<p>• What strategies will you use to build a bridge between data skills and real-world applications?</p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px;\">\r\n<p>➡️ Find the full details in the <a href=\"https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-2026/units/3/lessons/12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Lesson 12 lesson plan</a>.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>"
  },
